From: MCC45TR <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gdsc: remove initialized domains on registration failure

Remove initialized genpds when a later initialization, parent link or OF
provider registration fails. Unlink parents before removing domains and
skip holes in the domain array. The failing init has not registered a
genpd.

The initialized-domain unwind follows Konrad Dybcio's required-domain RFC
12/16. Its wider DVFS and rail-voter changes are not needed for this fix.
Controller PM references and physical power recovery remain separate work;
this cleanup does not qualify a camera provider for activation.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20261014-topic-qc_clk_dvfs-v1-12-3041b788e9f7@oss.qualcomm.com/
Signed-off-by: MCC45TR <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/gdsc.c | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/gdsc.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/gdsc.c
index 1b7317c0cd978214db8038ba4fa6b7b1b5b5298b..42efc3efde0933117713ba6bf0d89f8e8ef0e9fc 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gdsc.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gdsc.c
@@ -681,6 +681,7 @@ int gdsc_register(struct gdsc_desc *desc,
 	struct device *dev = desc->dev;
 	struct gdsc **scs = desc->scs;
 	size_t num = desc->num;
+	size_t initialized = 0;
 
 	/* Reject unsupported PM contracts before any domain register is touched. */
 	for (i = 0; i < num; i++) {
@@ -738,8 +739,9 @@ int gdsc_register(struct gdsc_desc *desc,
 			scs[i]->controller_dev = dev;
 		ret = gdsc_init(scs[i]);
 		if (ret)
-			return ret;
+			goto err_remove_domains;
 		data->domains[i] = &scs[i]->pd;
+		initialized = i + 1;
 	}
 
 	/* Add subdomains */
@@ -757,10 +759,17 @@ int gdsc_register(struct gdsc_desc *desc,
 			goto err_pm_subdomain_remove;
 	}
 
-	return of_genpd_add_provider_onecell(dev->of_node, data);
+	ret = of_genpd_add_provider_onecell(dev->of_node, data);
+	if (!ret)
+		return 0;
 
 err_pm_subdomain_remove:
 	gdsc_pm_subdomain_remove(desc, i);
+err_remove_domains:
+	while (initialized--) {
+		if (scs[initialized])
+			pm_genpd_remove(&scs[initialized]->pd);
+	}
 
 	return ret;
 }
